====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|nautical}} The act of [[#Verb|gybing]].
## A [[sudden]] [[shift#Noun|shift]] of a [[sail#Noun|sail]]'s [[angle#Noun|angle]], or a sudden [[change#Noun|change]] in the [[direction]] that a [[vessel]] is [[sail#Verb|sailing]] in.
## A [[manoeuvre#Noun|manoeuvre]] in which the [[stern#Noun|stern]] of a [[sailing vessel]] [[cross#Verb|crosses]] the [[wind#Noun|wind]], typically resulting in the [[forceful]] and sudden [[sweep#Noun|sweep]] of the [[boom#Noun|boom]] from one side of the vessel to the other.
##* {{quote-book|en|author=Tim Davison|chapter=Symmetric Spinnakers|title=Skipper’s Cockpit Racing Guide: For Dinghies, Keelboats and Yachts|location=London|publisher={{w|Adlard Coles Nautical}}|year=2014|page=24|pageurl=https://books.google.com.sg/books?id=DfsqAwAAQBAJ&pg=PA24|isbn=978-1-4729-0031-9|passage=The key to a good '''gybe''' is to bring the spinnaker round to the old weather side before you begin, and then to steer to keep some wind in the kite.}}
# {{lb|en|by extension}} A sudden change in [[approach#Noun|approach]] or direction; [[vacillation]].

